      "side": 1,
      "message": "That \u0027else\u0027 is wrong, but I don\u0027t the proposed fix is correct.\n\nThe if clause handles SOP -\u003e Cable Reset, and the only type that does not handle is TCPCI_MSG_TX_BIST_MODE_2. And, that case is a \"don\u0027t care\" for the sync packets as it\u0027s just a continuous 1/0s bit pattern. I think the correct fix is to drop the \u0027else\u0027 portion of this check.\n\nenum tcpci_msg_type {\n\tTCPCI_MSG_SOP \u003d 0,\n\tTCPCI_MSG_SOP_PRIME \u003d 1,\n\tTCPCI_MSG_SOP_PRIME_PRIME \u003d 2,\n\tTCPCI_MSG_SOP_DEBUG_PRIME \u003d 3,\n\tTCPCI_MSG_SOP_DEBUG_PRIME_PRIME \u003d 4,\n\t/* Only a valid register setting for TRANSMIT */\n\tTCPCI_MSG_TX_HARD_RESET \u003d 5,\n\tTCPCI_MSG_CABLE_RESET \u003d 6,\n\t/* Only a valid register setting for TRANSMIT */\n\tTCPCI_MSG_TX_BIST_MODE_2 \u003d 7,\n\tTCPCI_MSG_INVALID \u003d 0xf,\n};",
